 | `positive`           | OPTIONAL, but if you have a positive lab-control you'd like to compare results you can place that sample (the value in the sample column for the control) name for any non-lab controls. See example samplesheet as a reference                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                             |
 | `negative`           | OPTIONAL, but if you have a negative lab-control you'd like to compare results you can place that sample (the value in the sample column for the control) name for any non-lab controls. See example samplesheet as a reference                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                             |
 
+In Addition, you can provide metadata in one of two ways:
+
+1. Provide a `--meta` parameter with the path to a metadata CSV file. This file must have a `sample` column that matches the `sample` column in the samplesheet. The metadata will be used in the report and can be used for filtering and other downstream analysis.
+2. Add metadata directly into the samplesheet as additional columns. These columns will be added to the report and can be used for filtering and other downstream analysis. The metadata CSV file provided in `--meta` will take priority over any additional columns in the samplesheet if there are any conflicts.
+
+| Column               | Used in Multi Run Analysis Report | Description                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               |
+| -------------------- | --------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
+| `sample`             | Yes                               | **MANDATORY** Custom sample name. This entry will be identical for multiple sequencing libraries/runs from the same sample. Spaces in sample names are automatically converted to underscores (`_`).                                                                                                                                                                                                                      |
+| `run_id`             | Yes                               | OPTIONAL Run identifier. This can be used to group samples by run in the report. If not provided, all samples will be grouped together.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   |
+| `latitude`           | Yes                               | OPTIONAL Latitude of the sample collection site. This can be used for geospatial analysis in the report.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                  |
+| `longitude`          | Yes                               | OPTIONAL Longitude of the sample collection site. This can be used for geospatial analysis in the report.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                 |
+| `collection_time`    | Yes                               | OPTIONAL Time of sample collection. This can be used for temporal analysis in the report `report/all.odr.html`. Format must be: `YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS` e.g. `3/12/24 9:45`                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                 |
+| `....Other Metadata` | Yes                               | OPTIONAL Any other metadata columns can be added to the samplesheet or provided in a separate metadata CSV file. These will be included in the report and can be used for filtering and other downstream analysis. The metadata CSV file provided in `--meta` will take priority over any additional columns in the samplesheet if there are any conflicts. Examples would be things like: altitude, depth, comments, etc |
+
 An [example samplesheet](../examples/Samplesheet.csv) has been provided with the pipeline alongside some demo data.
 
+An [example ODR](https://jhuapl-bio.github.io/taxtriage/) has also been provided with the pipeline to show how the metadata is used in the report and how the different sample types are displayed. See the **Sample Metadata & Map tabs**.
+
 ## Running the pipeline
 
 The typical command for running the pipeline is as follows:
